@startuml
!include theme.iuml
allowmixing
title Private manual collection and read-only reference DTOs
hide empty members
class "RequestModel\n(request view)" as RequestModel <<reference>>
' @class backend.schemas.EntryCreate
class EntryCreate {
  text: StoredText
  entry_type: Word | Phrase | Sentence
  language; review_status
  lexical_category
  glosses; category; source_location
  notes; contributor
  valid_lexical_metadata(): Self
}
' @class backend.schemas.EntryPatch
class EntryPatch {
  editable fields: optional
  reject_null_fields(): Self
}
' @class backend.schemas.DatasetEntry
class DatasetEntry {
  id; text; entry_type
  french_gloss; english_gloss
  category; source_location; notes
  audio_filename; contributor; timestamp
  language; review_status; lexical_category
}
' @class backend.schemas.DatasetResponse
class DatasetResponse {
  total: int
  by_category: dict[str, int]
  by_type: dict[str, int]
  by_review_status: dict[str, int]
}
' @class backend.schemas.DictionaryEntry
class DictionaryEntry {
  id; text; aliases
  language: francanglais
  english_gloss; origin; topic
  source_document; source_line
}
' @class backend.schemas.DictionaryResponse
class DictionaryResponse {
  total; matched; offset; limit
  sources: list[str]
}
' @class backend.schemas.HealthResponse
class HealthResponse {
  status: ok
  mode: compiler
}
' @class backend.schemas.MetadataResponse
class MetadataResponse {
  categories: list[str]
  entry_types: list[str]
  lexical_categories: list[str]
  dataset_languages: list[str]
}
' @class backend.collection.CollectionError
class CollectionError {
  status_code: int
  detail: str
  __init__(status_code, detail)
}
class Exception <<external>>
rectangle "collection.py <<module>>\nlist_entries(), create_entry()\nedit_entry(), remove_entry()" as Collection
rectangle "dictionary.py <<module>>\nparse_dictionary(), load_dictionary()\nlist_dictionary(), headword_aliases()" as Dictionary
EntryCreate --|> RequestModel
EntryPatch --|> RequestModel
CollectionError --|> Exception
DatasetResponse "0..*" --> "0..*" DatasetEntry : entries
DictionaryResponse "0..*" --> "0..100" DictionaryEntry : entries
Dictionary ..> DictionaryEntry : parses supplied Markdown rows
Dictionary ..> DictionaryResponse : search and pagination
Dictionary ..> CollectionError : raises safe 503 on load failure
Collection ..> EntryCreate : validates create
Collection ..> EntryPatch : applies changed fields
Collection ..> DatasetResponse : returns list / selected-project counts
Collection ..> CollectionError : raises 404 / 409 / 422
note bottom of EntryPatch
  At least one field; explicit null is rejected.
  Omitted fields survive unchanged.
  ID, timestamp and audio are not editable.
end note
legend bottom
  The six response DTOs directly extend pydantic.BaseModel.
  EntryCreate/EntryPatch inherit extra=forbid via RequestModel.
  DatasetEntry is an API DTO, not the storage representation:
  Authenticated storage serializes dictionaries to private SQLite JSON rows.
  Desktop fallback helpers still persist dictionaries as CSV.
  Reference entries are read-only, not approved corpus entries.
  Their etymological origin does not supply a French gloss or POS.
  Pydantic response values inherit model_validate()/model_dump().
endlegend
@enduml
